# Cargo.lock IS committed. The usual "libraries don't commit a lockfile" advice
# does not apply: this crate ships a cdylib that has to be binary-compatible
# with a specific host build, and the pinned git revs only fix `ocs_plugin_api`
# and `acadrust` — every transitive crates.io dep would otherwise re-resolve on
# each CI run and land a different ahash/nalgebra/rkyv inside the released .dll.
# internal working draft for issue #157 — not for the public repo
docs/landxml-import-proposal.md

